<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00VM">Example <span data-tag="00VM">3.2.2.3</span>.</a> For $n \geq 0$, the geometric realization $| \Delta ^ n / \operatorname{\partial \Delta }^ n |$ can be obtained from the topological $n$-simplex $| \Delta ^ n |$ by collapsing the boundary $| \operatorname{\partial \Delta }^ n |$ to a point (or by adding a new base point, in the degenerate case $n = 0$). It follows that $| \Delta ^ n / \operatorname{\partial \Delta }^ n |$ is homeomorphic to a sphere of dimension $n$. </p>
